Covered: the `5400 → "1h30m"` example, each unit alone, all four together (`93784 → "1d2h3m4s"`), zero-unit omission in the middle (`86401 → "1d1s"`), both edge cases, and a `parse_duration(format_duration(n)) == n` round-trip. I also round-tripped every 7th value from 0 to 200,000 in a scratch script (not part of the suite) — all exact.
